# Repository Pattern

```kotlin
@Inject
class {Feature}RepositoryImpl(
    private val remoteDataSource: {Feature}RemoteDataSource,
    private val userLocalDataSource: UserLocalDataSource,
    private val mapper: {Feature}Mapper
) : {Feature}Repository {

    override fun get{Items}(): Flow<Result<List<{Entity}>>> = flow {
        emit(Result.Loading)
        try {
            val token = requireAuthToken()
            val response = remoteDataSource.get{Items}(token)
            emit(Result.Success(mapper.mapToDomainList(response.data)))
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            emit(Result.Error(e, ApiErrorHandler.extractMessage(e)))
        }
    }

    private suspend fun requireAuthToken(): String {
        return userLocalDataSource.getAuthToken()
            ?: throw ApiException.AuthenticationException("No auth token")
    }
}
```

## Rules
- Interface in `domain/repository/`, impl in `data/repository/`
- List endpoints return `Flow<Result<List<T>>>`, single-item returns `suspend Result<T>`
- Always emit `Result.Loading` first in flow builders
- Get auth token via `userLocalDataSource.getAuthToken()`
- Map DTOs to domain entities via `{Feature}Mapper` — never return DTOs
- Error handling: catch `Exception`, use `ApiErrorHandler.extractMessage(e)`
